     1,
     "Dear All,\r<br>\r<br>I have 2 tumor samples and 2 control samples and want to find\r<br>alternative splicing.\r<br>\r<br>After I got the FIRMA score, Could I use limma to find the alternative\r<br>splicing?\r<br>\r<br>Before using limma, I did log2 scale to FIRMA score. But I found there\r<br>are a lot of negative value in data set. It is common?\r<br>\r<br>Original Firma score:\r<br>head(exFirma)\r<br>  unitName groupName unit group cell RD2009092839 RD2009092840\r<br>RD2009092841\r<br>1  6838637   4304927    1     1    1    0.4586444    0.2794902\r<br>1.8639828\r<br>2  6838637   4330595    1     2    2    0.6102609    0.9152724\r<br>1.3151890\r<br>3  6838637   4356771    1     3    3    1.6570473    0.1941053\r<br>1.3088931\r<br>4  6838637   4366326    1     4    4    0.7417230    1.8255262\r<br>0.7095107\r<br>5  6838637   4367951    1     5    5    1.0001453    1.3591065\r<br>0.6875097\r<br>6  6838637   4396376    1     6    6    1.4089704    0.4405679\r<br>1.1440083\r<br>  RD2009092842\r<br>1    1.3710542\r<br>2    1.3612753\r<br>3    0.8766123\r<br>4    0.6292946\r<br>5    1.2785655\r<br>6    0.6761603\r<br>\r<br>log2 score:\r<br> &gt; head(exFirma)\r<br>  unitName groupName unit group cell  RD2009092839 RD2009092840\r<br>RD2009092841\r<br>1  6838637   4304927    1     1    1 -1.1245521013   -1.8391304\r<br>0.8983885\r<br>2  6838637   4330595    1     2    2 -0.7125019273   -0.1277269\r<br>0.3952701\r<br>3  6838637   4356771    1     3    3  0.7286147599   -2.3650883\r<br>0.3883473\r<br>4  6838637   4366326    1     4    4 -0.4310475869    0.8683124\r<br>-0.4951036\r<br>5  6838637   4367951    1     5    5  0.0002096316    0.4426586\r<br>-0.5405480\r<br>6  6838637   4396376    1     6    6  0.4946412584   -1.1825638\r<br>0.1940975\r<br>  RD2009092842\r<br>1    0.4552856\r<br>2    0.4449589\r<br>3   -0.1899892\r<br>4   -0.6681926\r<br>5    0.3545261\r<br>6   -0.5645628\r<br>\r<br>Thanks\r<br>\r<br>Hailei"
